From 24a1b8984ebd4bf07b4bf07eaf387c212ec1819b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefan <kloterstefan@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 03:20:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/19] tests: the Vizz installer over a unit running Vizz 1.0
 (backup, install, conversion)

Skiff 2.0's installer takes a complete backup before it installs over
firmware before 2.0 and converts what 2.0 can't read after it. A unit
running Vizz 1.0 (FM-1_810, "FELUCCA v1.0", Skiff 1.4's formats) must
get both. Tested on the one-file installer as it ships:

- tests/vizz10_fixture.sh: such a unit made by Vizz 1.0's own code (a
  checkout of Skiff v1.4 with the vizz-1.0 patches): the editor's INFO
  reply and a complete backup of its flash: the music (SKF3), the
  settings (PER4, Skiff's mark; SEQ MIDI OUT OFF, T2 on channel 10),
  slot 1 saved by Vizz 1.0 (SKF3), slot 3 an older Skiff's that 1.4 kept
  (SKF2), a user sound, the patterns -> tests/vizz10_unit.json
- web/test_vizz_installer.mjs: the installer in Chromium (Playwright),
  Web MIDI a simulated unit (the update protocol as test_web.mjs's
  FakeFM1, the backup requests as the firmware answers them). Vizz 1.0:
  the backup first, saved as Vizz-backup-DATE.json bit for bit, the
  question, the install, then exactly the converter's write-back (slot
  3 as SKF4, the FM6 patches object) and the list; a Vizz 1.x by its
  identity whatever its version says; Skiff 1.4 and a development
  build by the version; Vizz 2.0 and Skiff 2.0.1 installed with no
  backup. 2.0 reads Vizz 1.0's settings as Skiff's (SEQ MIDI OUT OFF
  and the channels kept). Skipped without Playwright.
- run_tests.sh: makes the installer of build/felucca.fwsc and runs it,
  after the converter's own tests (it needs build/conv/conv.wasm)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011Z5NrMFizGcfqt3zdrJXAX
